        "route": "/minerals/common/ores/antimony-ore",
        "body": "# Antimony Ore\n\n## Effect\nAntimony Ore is a brittle, crystalline metal-bearing ore that enhances hardness and structural integrity when alloyed. It is rarely used alone but is critical in reinforcing softer metals.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nKnown as the *“Bone of the Earth,”* antimony was believed by ancient smiths to give metals their “spine.” While fragile in isolation, it grants resilience to those it strengthens.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- Brittle and unstable in raw form  \n- Breaks easily under stress  \n- Essential for strengthening alloys  \n- Requires careful refinement  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Antimony Ingot]]\n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot\n- Notes: Fragile structure leads to material loss if overheated\n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- [[Pewter Ingot]]\n- Future reinforced alloys\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Slightly improves structural stability of enchanted items  \n- Helps prevent deformation under magical stress  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It does not endure — it ensures that others do.\"*"
