        "body": "# Moonstone Ore\n\n## Effect\nMoonstone Ore carries lunar resonance, shifting subtly in response to light cycles and magical presence. It stabilises and harmonises magical energy rather than amplifying or suppressing it.\n\n---\n## Appearance\nMoonstone Ore appears as pale, semi-translucent stone veined with soft silver and faint blue hues. It emits a gentle, diffused glow that subtly brightens and dims, as if responding to an unseen cycle.\n\nWithin the ore, faint patterns resembling drifting light or slow-moving ripples can be seen, giving the impression that the material is quietly alive with lunar energy.\n\n---\n## Lore\nMoonstone forms where celestial light meets the physical world in cycles — waxing and waning with unseen forces. It is said to reflect not just the moon above, but the balance between Light and Dark within the world itself.\n\n---\n\n## Material & Crafting Traits\n- Responds to ambient light and magical cycles  \n- Stabilises fluctuating magical energy  \n- Maintains structural integrity under magical stress  \n- Often found in regions touched by celestial influence  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Moonstone Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Notes: Refinement is most stable under controlled or natural light cycles  \n\n---\n\n## Alloy Use\n- Celestial or arcane-balanced alloys (future)\n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- High affinity with **Celestial and Arcane** magic  \n- Stabilises multi-effect enchantments  \n- Reduces magical volatility  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It does not choose a side — it reflects them both.\"*"
