        "body": "# Red Duranium Ore\n\n## Effect\nRed Duranium Ore is a corrupted evolution of Duranium Ore, transformed by the extreme heat, bloodshed, and violent energy surrounding the Zahram Peaks.\n\nUnlike normal Duranium, the ore actively absorbs heat and vitality from its environment, storing it as unstable internal energy.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nRed Duranium Ore appears as dense, dark metallic stone threaded with deep crimson veins that pulse faintly beneath the surface.\n\nThese veins glow brighter when exposed to combat, heat, or living creatures, giving the ore the appearance of a slow, burning heartbeat trapped within stone.\n\nFragments of the ore remain unnaturally warm even during cold nights within the desert.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nRed Duranium Ore forms only within the Zahram Peaks, a mountain range hidden deep within the Rahzakar Dunes — known in Common as the Ember Dunes.\n\nThe region is infamous for its extreme heat, blood-red sandstorms, and monstrous creatures that move beneath the dunes waiting for prey. Over centuries, Duranium Ore exposed to the violence and environmental pressure of the region mutates into Red Duranium.\n\nMany believe the mountains themselves are alive, feeding the ore through conflict and death.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Converts environmental heat into internal energy  \n- Reacts to nearby living creatures  \n- Extremely dense and difficult to extract  \n- Highly unstable during refinement if improperly handled  \n- Maintains heat for long periods of time  \n\n---\n\n## Formation\n- Originates from: [[Duranium Ore]]  \n- Requires:\n  - Extreme environmental heat  \n  - Prolonged exposure to violence and death  \n  - Continuous energy saturation from the Zahram Peaks  \n\n---\n\n## Refinement\n- Smelts into: [[Red Duranium Ingot]]  \n- Ratio: 4 Ore → 1 Ingot  \n- Requires specialised high-temperature forge  \n- Standard forges risk catastrophic failure during smelting  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Strong affinity with **Fire** and **Death**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Aggressive enchantments  \n  - Burn and decay effects  \n  - Sustain and vitality-drain abilities  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"The mountain does not forge the ore — it feeds it.\"*"
