        "body": "# Red Duranium Ingot\n\n## Effect\nRed Duranium is a corrupted evolution of Duranium, forged through exposure to immense heat, bloodshed, and violent energy. It retains the adaptive resilience of Duranium while converting absorbed force into aggression, regeneration, and destructive output.\n\n---\n\n## Appearance\nRed Duranium Ingots are dark metallic bars streaked with deep crimson veins that pulse slowly beneath the surface like molten blood.\n\nThe metal radiates faint heat constantly, and during combat or stress, the glow intensifies as energy moves throughout the ingot.\n\nWhen struck, the metal emits a deep resonance rather than a metallic clang.\n\n---\n\n## Lore\nRed Duranium is found only within the Zahram Peaks, surrounded by the deadly Rahzakar Dunes.\n\nOver countless years, Duranium exposed to the extreme conditions of the region mutates into a far more dangerous material. The constant cycle of death, predation, and heat saturates the ore with violent energy, transforming it into a living, reactive alloy.\n\nWeapons and armor forged from Red Duranium are feared for their hunger — growing stronger through prolonged combat and sustained conflict.\n\n---\n\n## Material Traits\n- Converts absorbed force into offensive energy  \n- Regenerates minor structural damage through heat and vitality  \n- Extremely resistant to physical and fire-based damage  \n- Can destabilise weaker wielders over time  \n- Performs best under sustained combat pressure  \n\n---\n\n## Variant Transformation\n- Originates from: [[Duranium Ingot]]  \n- Requires:\n  - Red Duranium Ore  \n  - High-temperature forge  \n  - Controlled refinement process  \n\n---\n\n## Enchantment Use\n- Strong affinity with **Fire** and **Death**  \n- Enhances:\n  - Burn effects  \n  - Life-drain  \n  - Aggressive combat enchantments  \n- Less stable with defensive or purification enchantments  \n\n---\n\n## Combat Integration\n- +5 Damage Modifier  \n- +4 Armor Modifier  \n- Favours aggressive, sustain, and high-risk combat builds  \n\n---\n\n## Special Interaction\n- Becomes more effective during prolonged combat  \n- Regenerates minor damage slowly over time  \n- Reacts aggressively to nearby violence or bloodshed  \n- May influence emotionally unstable wielders  \n\n---\n\n## Acquisition\n- Found only within the Zahram Peaks  \n- Extraction requires surviving:\n  - The Rahzakar Dunes  \n  - Burrowing sand predators  \n  - Extreme environmental heat  \n  - Violent territorial creatures  \n\n---\n\n## Quote\n*\"It remembers every drop of blood that fed its fire.\"*"
